Description: stop the BubbleHelp watcher thread cooperatively
 ~BubbleHelp() killed its polling helper with kill_thread(), which on
 VOS takes the whole team, and it did so while holding the helper's own
 window lock - the helper takes that lock in short sections, so a
 wait-for-thread under that lock would deadlock. Set a volatile fQuit
 flag the helper's two poll loops check, reap with wait_for_thread()
 without holding the lock, then quit the window as before; the flag is
 initialised in the constructor and the startup wait honours it too.
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/ClipUp
